{"raw": {"https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/19719": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Professor of Social Work Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Social Work Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F156P Working Title Assistant Professor of Social Work FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary $56,000 - $59,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 9 Months Department Dept of Psychology, Social Work, and Counseling Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University seeks a tenure-track assistant professor to serve as the MSW Program Director and lead the development, accreditation, and administration of an online, asynchronous Master of Social Work ( MSW ) program. Responsibilities include teaching graduate social work courses at both the foundation and advanced levels; advising and mentoring students in their professional development and licensure preparation; leading curriculum development, program assessment, and CSWE accreditation activities; and collaborating with the Director of Practicum Education to support student field placements. The MSW Program Director will also provide service to the Department, University, and community, support program growth, ensure compliance with Council on Social Work Education ( CSWE ) standards, and advance Shepherd University\u2019s mission of preparing ethical, skilled social workers to serve diverse communities. As MSW Program Director, the successful candidate must be able to maintain a regular physical presence on campus to provide program leadership, collaborate with faculty and staff, participate in university service, and support students and community partners. Minimum Qualifications Master of Social Work ( MSW ) degree from a CSWE -accredited program. Ph.D. in Social Work or Doctor of Social Work ( DSW ) degree from a CSWE -accredited program. A minimum of five years of post- MSW professional social work practice experience. A minimum of two years of teaching experience in a CSWE -accredited BSW or MSW program. Experience developing and/or revising social work courses at the BSW or MSW level. Preferred Qualifications Professional Licensure ( LGSW , LCSW , or LICSW ). Experience in both undergraduate and graduate social work education. Expertise in clinical social work practice or other high-need practice areas. Experience with online teaching and curriculum design. Ability to begin employment in January 2027 Posting Date 09/01/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary For guaranteed consideration, please apply by November 1, 2026. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Wide range of health insurance and other benefits 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/19692": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Education", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Professor of Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F158P Working Title Assistant Professor of Education FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Beginning at $55,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 9 Months Department School of Education Job Summary/Basic Function The School of Education at Shepherd University invites applications for a full-time, tenured track, Assistant Professor in the School of Education beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in elementary education, literacy and/or special education, engage in scholarly research, advise students, supervise field experiences, and contribute to service at the school, and university levels, and advising. Courses may be face-to-face, hybrid, or online. Evening teaching may be required. Minimum Qualifications Earned Doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Elementary Education, Special Education or closely related field Minimum of 3 years of successful teaching experience in a K\u20136 setting. Evidence of scholarly potential or record (publications, conference presentations, etc.). Excellent communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications Reading/Literacy Specialist Special Education Certification Experience teaching at the college/university level. Familiarity with edTPA or other performance-based assessments. Experience supervising teacher candidates in field placements. Ability to integrate technology into instruction and field supervision. Posting Date 10/02/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary For guaranteed consideration, please apply by November 13, 2026. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Wide range of health insurance and other benefits 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents The University does not provide sponsorship for employment visas, including H-1B, H-2B, E, TN, O, or similar work-authorized classifications, for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without current or future employer sponsorship. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of Professional References Optional Documents Resume VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/19635": {"title": "Clinical Instructor of Accounting", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Clinical Instructor of Accounting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Instructor of Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F157P Working Title Clinical Instructor of Accounting FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Begining at $64,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 9 Months Department Dept of Business and Sport Administration Job Summary/Basic Function The university invites applications for the position of Clinical Instructor of Accounting. Responsibilities include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels, university service, and advising. Courses may be face-to-face, hybrid, or online. Evening teaching may be required. Responsibilities will primarily include teaching accounting, but will also include support for business administration and finance courses in the undergraduate and/or graduate program, committee service, and advising responsibilities. The candidate will teach tax and coordinate student participation in the local VITA program. Courses may be face-to-face, hybrid, or online. However, they will primarily be in person. Evening teaching may be required. Minimum Qualifications Qualified candidates for the Accounting Clinical Instructor position must have a minimum of a Master\u2019s degree with CPA certification and experience in the field. The candidate must be able to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or the ability to obtain one. Posting Date 09/29/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. For more information, contact: Dr. Cindy Vance, Ph.D., CPA , Accounting Search Committee Chair via email at cvance@shepherd.edu . The position is open until November 1, 2026. The University does not provide sponsorship for employment visas, including H-1B, H-2B, E, TN, O, or similar work-authorized classifications, for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without current or future employer sponsorship. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of Professional References Optional Documents Resume VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/19312": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Professor of Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F155P Working Title Assistant Professor of Psychology FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary $55,000 - $58,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 9 Months Department Dept of Psychology, Social Work, and Counseling Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Psychology position, with an open area of specialization, beginning Fall 2027. The ideal candidate will have a doctoral degree in Psychology and a strong background in Psychological Science and a commitment to undergraduate education. Candidates should be able to teach the introductory course, Statistics, Research Methods, and courses in their area of specialization. The typical course load is four classes per semester. The Psychology program at Shepherd is a vibrant major with approximately 125 students and a strong record of preparing graduates for advanced study and professional careers. Minimum Qualifications The successful candidate must have completed a doctoral degree in Psychology or be ABD by the time of employment and demonstrate experience teaching at the college level. Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate will possess the ability to teach Introduction to Psychology, Statistics, Research Methods, and the undergraduate capstone. They will have experience engaging undergraduate students in the classroom and involving them in research activities. Posting Date 09/01/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary For guaranteed consideration, please apply by November 1, 2026. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Wide range of health insurance and other benefits 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/19311": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Environmental Science", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Professor of Environmental Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Environmental Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F154P Working Title Assistant Professor of Environmental Science FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary 60,000 - 63,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 9 Months Department Dept of Natural and Physical Sciences Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Natural and Physical Sciences at Shepherd University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Environmental Science with specialization in an Ecology-related field. The Department values student mentorship and experiential learning opportunities and seeks candidates who combine field and/or lab research in their teaching. Candidates excited about supporting undergraduate research and who are dedicated to high quality, innovative undergraduate education are encouraged to apply. The candidate will be expected to teach 3 lectures and associated labs per semester, hold office hours each week, and assist with student advising and mentorship. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level, postdoctoral experience, and/or experience mentoring undergraduate research students. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Environmental Science or closely related field, teaching experience at the undergraduate level, and a willingness to mentor undergraduate research students. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Environmental Science or closely related field and experience teaching Aquatic Science classes such as Oceanography, Limnology, and Stream Ecology, the ability to conduct research, preferably involving undergraduate students, and a willingness to mentor undergraduate research students in projects of their own. Posting Date 09/01/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Applicants should submit a cover letter; a curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy; a research statement that includes your approach to engaging undergraduate students; and the names and contact information (phone number, email address, mailing address) for three references. For guaranteed consideration, please apply by October 8, 2026. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Wide range of health insurance and other benefits 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Other Document 1 List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18799": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Business and Sport Administration", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Professor of Business and Sport Administration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Business and Sport Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F153P Working Title Assistant Professor of Business and Sport Administration FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Beginning at $56,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 9 Months Department Dept of Business and Sport Administration Job Summary/Basic Function Responsibilities include teaching in the Recreation and Sport Studies academic program and teaching cross-disciplinary classes in Business. Additional duties also include participation in scholarly activity and professional development; providing departmental, college, and university support through participation in campus and community events; and providing professional service through active participation on campus committees. Opportunities are also available to teach at the graduate level if qualified. Minimum Qualifications Earned Doctorate in the areas of Recreation, Sport, and/or Business Administration is required. Preferred Qualifications Minimum of three (3) years of teaching experience in the higher education environment, including a background in advising, research, service, and professional development at the University level, and knowledge and experience with national accreditation processes and assessment. Posting Date 07/22/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Priority will be given to applicants who submit their applications by August 30, 2026. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Anticipated starting date is January 2027. Electronically submit a letter of interest/application, CV, and teaching philosophy. Include contact information for three to five references. The letter of interest/application should include and highlight specific experience and qualifications as referenced in the job description. Wide range of health insurance and other benefits 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18691": {"title": "Adjunct \u2013 Communications, Public Speaking", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct \u2013 Communications, Public Speaking Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct \u2013 Communications, Public Speaking Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F152P Working Title Adjunct \u2013 Communications, Public Speaking FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Other Department School of the Arts and Media Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University seeks qualified adjunct instructors to teach COMM 202: Fundamentals of Speech in an in-person format. This three-credit course is a required core curriculum course focused on the skills of sending and receiving clear messages. Topics include audience analysis, message organization, listening awareness, communication apprehension, and the delivery of speeches in multiple formats. The University is especially interested in instructors who will provide students with meaningful face-to-face experience in public speaking. Many students who enroll in COMM 202 are future teachers or students preparing for careers that require confidence speaking in front of groups. For that reason, in-person instruction is essential to the goals of the course. Students should have regular opportunities to stand before their peers, practice prepared and impromptu communication, receive feedback, and build confidence in a supportive classroom environment. Responsibilities include teaching assigned in-person sections of COMM 202; preparing course materials and assignments aligned with course objectives; guiding students through communication exercises and speech preparation; evaluating student speeches and presentations; providing timely feedback; maintaining student records; and submitting grades according to university deadlines. The successful candidate will be a student-centered instructor who understands the importance of active practice, constructive feedback, and confidence-building in the development of effective oral communication skills. Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Communication, Speech Communication, Rhetoric, or a closely related field. Prior experience teaching, coaching, or mentoring students in public speaking, oral communication, presentation, performance, or related skills. Preferred Qualifications Prior college teaching experience Experience teaching public speaking or communication courses A demonstrated ability to support students who may experience anxiety or apprehension around public speaking Posting Date 07/01/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/16882": {"title": "Adjunct Contemporary Art and Theater Instructor", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct Contemporary Art and Theater Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Contemporary Art and Theater Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Shepherd University accepts applications for Adjunct Instructors on a continuous basis. Applications may be reviewed periodically as needs arise. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F139P Working Title Adjunct Contemporary Art and Theater Instructor FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Department Dept of Contemporary Art, Communications, and Theater Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in their subject field of specialization to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. Minimum Qualifications Graduate degree in field of specialization Preferred Qualifications Posting Date 10/20/2025 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/13496": {"title": "Adjunct Nursing Instructor", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct Nursing Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Nursing Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F018P Working Title Adjunct Nursing Instructor FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Department School of Nursing Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in their subject field of specialization to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. Minimum Qualifications BSN -prepared Rn with 2-5 years of experience or graduate degree in area of nursing specialty Unencumbered RN multistate or WV RN license Preferred Qualifications Certification in area of specialty preferred Clinical scheduling may occur during weekday or weekend hours. Posting Date 11/10/2021 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/12152": {"title": "Adjunct \u2013 First Year Experience", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct \u2013 First Year Experience Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct \u2013 First Year Experience Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F087P Working Title Adjunct \u2013 First Year Experience FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Other Department Dept of First Year Experience Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in their subject field of specialization to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. Minimum Qualifications Graduate degree in your subject field of specialization. Preferred Qualifications - Posting Date 06/16/2023 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Shepherd University accepts applications for Adjunct Instructors on a continuous basis. Applications may be reviewed periodically as needs arise. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of Professional References VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/12083": {"title": "Adjunct - APST", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct - APST Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct - APST Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F100P Working Title Adjunct - APST FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Other Department Interdisciplinary Studies Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in their subject field of specialization to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. This position will be responsible for teaching APST 358/558 Appalachian Literature . Minimum Qualifications MA in Appalachian Studies Preferred Qualifications - Posting Date 04/19/2024 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Equivalent combination of experience and training which provides the required knowledge, skills and abilities may be considered as meeting the minimum qualifications, at the direction of the hiring supervisor. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of Professional References Optional Documents Cover Letter VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/12045": {"title": "Adjunct \u2013 Music", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct \u2013 Music Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct \u2013 Music Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F099P Working Title Adjunct \u2013 Music FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Other Department School of the Arts and Media Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in their subject field of specialization to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. Minimum Qualifications graduate degree Preferred Qualifications - Posting Date 04/16/2024 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Equivalent combination of experience and training which provides the required knowledge, skills and abilities may be considered as meeting the minimum qualifications, at the direction of the hiring supervisor. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of Professional References Optional Documents Cover Letter VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/11665": {"title": "Adjunct \u2013 Education", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct \u2013 Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct \u2013 Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F096P Working Title Adjunct \u2013 Education FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Other Department School of Education Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in the field of education to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. High need areas are in science and mathematics pedagogy in both elementary and secondary placements. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. Minimum Qualifications Graduate degree in field of education Preferred Qualifications Posting Date 02/01/2024 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/8291": {"title": "Adjunct \u2013 Biology", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct \u2013 Biology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct \u2013 Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F081P Working Title Adjunct \u2013 Biology FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Other Department Dept of Biology Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University Depar