lifications Graduate degree in your subject field of specialization. Preferred Qualifications Posting Date 02/04/2022 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Letter of Reference 2 VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/8128": {"title": "Adjunct Graduate Faculty: MAT and MACI", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct Graduate Faculty: MAT and MACI Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Graduate Faculty: MAT and MACI Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F027P Working Title Adjunct Graduate Faculty: MAT and MACI FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Department Graduate Studies Job Summary/Basic Function MAT seeks adjuncts who are interested in teaching graduate students who are seeking an initial teacher certification for those with bachelor\u2019s degrees in selected fields. MA \u2013 CI seek adjuncts who are interested in teaching graduate students who are seeking improve their quality of instruction and better prepare them for leadership roles within their school districts. The Division of Graduate Studies and Continuing Education seeks qualified adjuncts to teach courses in a number of select disciplines within its degree and certificate programs. Graduate studies at Shepherd University provides quality content with a strong emphasis on career preparation. Graduate programs offered respond to the career goals of its students, the needs of local and regional employers for highly qualified professionals, and the ability of the university to provide quality graduate education. Members of the graduate faculty must be qualified in their subject matter (normally with a terminal degree in their field) and must demonstrate a pattern of sustained professional activity. Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in the field of expertise. Preferred Qualifications Posting Date 01/25/2022 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of Professional References Optional Documents Resume Transcripts Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/8127": {"title": "Adjunct Mathematics", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F024P Working Title Adjunct Mathematics FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Faculty Advertised Salary Position Status Part Time Appointment Length Department Dept of Computer Science, Mathematics and Engineering Job Summary/Basic Function Shepherd University invites individuals who hold a graduate degree in their subject field of specialization to apply for consideration for an adjunct instructor position. Classes may be scheduled in day or evening hours. Shepherd supports a mentoring and teaching/learning program for adjunct instructors. Minimum Qualifications Graduate degree in your subject field of specialization. Preferred Qualifications Posting Date 12/07/2021 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/8122": {"title": "University Supervisor of Student Teachers", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | University Supervisor of Student Teachers Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help University Supervisor of Student Teachers Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory criminal records background check. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number F009P Working Title University Supervisor of Student Teachers FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Advertised Salary Position Status Appointment Length Department School of Education Job Summary/Basic Function The University Supervisor of Student Teachers is a professional whose concern is to see that every successful student teacher is ready to be a first-year teacher. The supervisor must seek evidence that the student possesses the disposition, knowledge, and the performance characteristics expected of a teacher education student in the Shepherd University program. The University Supervisor if Student Teachers shall: (1) develop and maintain a professional working relationship among cooperating teachers, school administrators, school staff, and students; (2) observe the performance by the students and give guidance designed to make him/her more effective; (3) confer with the student and cooperating teacher on topics pertinent to the student\u2019s performance; (4) assist the student and cooperating teacher regarding problems that may arise during the practicum period (5) assign and submit a grade for student teaching no later than two days after the last day scheduled for student teaching. This role is part-time and the load of student teachers varies by semester. Availability during public school operation hours (usually 7 a.m.-4:30 p.m., varies depending on location) is essential. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree with a minimum of 3 years experience as a certified teacher in the content area for which they would be supervising. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in education with a minimum of 3 years experience as a certified teacher in the content area for which they would be supervising. Posting Date 10/20/2021 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV 25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/8121": {"title": "Adjunct Sociology Instructor", "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Adjunct Sociology Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Sociology Instructor Bookmark this